# Own-wording spells of Valda's Spire of Secrets (2014 rules), part B.
HL = "\n\n**At Higher Levels.** "
TEXT = {
"Delay": ["60 ft. Wisdom save or the target drops to last in initiative from the next round on.",
 "60 ft. You briefly slow time for a creature you see. It makes a Wisdom save or moves to last place in the initiative order from the start of the next round onward."],
"Demand": ["Unlimited range, Concentration, 8 hours. Send a 25 word message, and optionally force a suggestion with a Wisdom save.",
 "Unlimited range, Concentration, 8 hours. You send a message of 25 words or fewer to a creature you know. It hears the message in its mind, knows you sent it if it knows you, and can answer at once the same way. Any creature with Intelligence 1 or higher understands it. The message crosses any distance and even planes, but to another plane there is a 5 percent chance it fails to arrive. You can include a reasonable-sounding course of action. The target then makes a Wisdom save or must follow it for the duration, as with Suggestion."],
"Dire Charm": ["Touch, 10 days. Charm a Humanoid (Wisdom save, Disadvantage unless you fight it). Permanent at 8th level.",
 "Touch, 10 days. You try to charm a Humanoid you see in range. It makes a Wisdom save, with Disadvantage unless you or your companions are fighting it. On a failure it is charmed by you until the spell ends and regards you as a friendly acquaintance. If you or your companions harm it, it can save again. When the spell ends, it knows you charmed it." + HL + "With an 8th-level slot or higher the duration is until dispelled."],
"Dire Warning": ["Self. Receive a 6 word message from your future self, which you must send back with a 10 minute ritual.",
 "Self. You receive a message of up to 6 words from your future self, warning of a critical threat or pointing to a useful path. Later, once you learn why the message was sent, you must perform a 10-minute ritual to send it back to your past self. After casting, you cannot cast this spell again until you do the ritual, or until a week passes if you never learn the reason. If you receive no message, you never complete the ritual in the future, perhaps because you die or are prevented."],
"Distort Gravity": ["Touch, Concentration, 1 hour. A surface up to 60 ft square pulls creatures within 15 ft of it as if it were the ground.",
 "Touch, Concentration, 1 hour. You bend gravity on a non-horizontal surface you touch so that it attracts creatures and objects within 15 feet as if it were the ground. The surface can be up to 60 feet square and can wrap around a structure if its shape allows. Creatures can walk on it as on level ground, even if it is vertical or upside down. When the spell ends, everything on it falls."],
"Eldritch Orb": ["Cantrip, 60 ft. Ranged spell attack for 1d8 force, and creatures within 5 ft of the target make a Dexterity save for half.",
 "60 ft. You fling a ball of eldritch energy at a creature or object in range. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit the target takes 1d8 force damage, and each other creature within 5 feet of it makes a Dexterity save, taking half as much damage on a failure.\n\nThe damage rises by 1d8 at level 5, 11 and 17."],
"Elemental Curse": ["Touch, Concentration, 1 minute. Constitution save or the target gains vulnerability to acid, cold, fire, lightning or thunder.",
 "Touch, Concentration, 1 minute. A spark leaps from your finger to a creature you touch and spreads across its skin in bright cracks. It makes a Constitution save or is cursed. While cursed it is vulnerable to your choice of acid, cold, fire, lightning or thunder damage. If it resists that type, it loses the Resistance instead. If it is immune, it is treated as only resistant. Remove Curse ends it."],
"Evasiveness": ["Touch, Concentration, 1 hour. Target's AC becomes at least 20 and it has Advantage on Dexterity saves.",
 "Touch, Concentration, 1 hour. You touch a willing creature. It gains a superhuman knack for dodging. Its AC becomes 20 if it was lower, whatever armor it wears, and it has Advantage on Dexterity saves."],
"Exhume": ["Self. Raise one pile of Humanoid bones in a 20 ft square (1d4 in a graveyard).",
 "Self. Choose an unoccupied 20-foot square in range with solid earth beneath it. The spell fails on the upper floor of a building. One pile of Humanoid bones rises from the ground in that square. In a burial place such as a graveyard, mausoleum or barrow, 1d4 piles rise instead. The ground itself is not disturbed."],
"Eye of Anubis": ["Cantrip, 60 ft. Ranged spell attack for 1d8 necrotic and the target cannot Disengage. A second beam at level 5.",
 "60 ft. A beam of dark moonlight streaks from your left eye at a creature in range. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit the target takes 1d8 necrotic damage and cannot take the Disengage action until the end of your next turn.\n\nAt level 5 you fire a second beam from your right eye. The first beam's damage becomes 2d8 at level 11, and the second beam's at level 17."],
"Eye of Ra": ["Cantrip, 60 ft. Ranged spell attack for 1d8 radiant and the target cannot Hide. A second beam at level 5.",
 "60 ft. A beam of furious radiance erupts from your right eye at a creature you see in range. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit the target takes 1d8 radiant damage and cannot take the Hide action until the end of your next turn.\n\nAt level 5 you fire a second beam from your left eye. The first beam's damage becomes 2d8 at level 11, and the second beam's at level 17."],
"False Vision": ["Touch, 8 hours. Hide a creature, place or object from divination and feed the diviner false information.",
 "Touch, 8 hours. You hide a willing creature, a place, or an object no larger than 10 feet on a side from divination magic. If the target is targeted by divination or seen through a scrying sensor, you can show the diviner false information of your choice, as long as you are conscious. The target can appear in other circumstances, in false locations, or be undetectable."],
"Finger Guns": ["Cantrip, Bonus Action, 1 minute. Use your action to shoot a ranged spell attack within 60 ft for 1d8 force. It counts as a firearm.",
 "Self, 1 minute. You extend your forefinger and thumb like a gun. For the duration you can use your action to make a ranged spell attack against a creature you see within 60 feet, dealing 1d8 force damage on a hit. It needs no ammunition but counts as a firearm for spells and effects that affect firearms.\n\nThe damage rises by 1d8 at level 5, 11 and 17."],
"Flawed Reconstruction": ["Touch. Heal 4d6, but the target's hit point maximum drops by the same amount until a Long Rest, and it is scarred.",
 "Touch. You stitch the wounds of a willing creature, which regains 4d6 hit points. The mending is imperfect: its hit point maximum drops by the same amount until it finishes a Long Rest, and it keeps permanent scars." + HL + "The healing rises by 4d6 for each slot level above 1."],
"Flesh Ripper": ["Cantrip, 30 ft. Ranged spell attack for 1d8 piercing, and the target needs a Strength save to move over 30 ft from you.",
 "30 ft. A spectral meat hook and chain flies at a creature you choose. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit the target takes 1d8 piercing damage. Until the start of your next turn it must make a Strength save to move more than 30 feet from you, and on a failure it cannot move until your turn starts. The effect ends if you are more than 30 feet away.\n\nThe damage rises by 1d8 at level 5, 11 and 17."],
"Force Buckler": ["Cantrip, Bonus Action, self, 1 round. +2 AC from a force shield until your next turn. Ends if you are hit.",
 "Self, 1 round. A see-through but visible field of force springs from a prepared gauntlet worth at least 5 gp. Until the start of your next turn it gives +2 AC as if you wielded a shield. It ends early if you are hit by an attack."],
"Force Dart": ["Cantrip, 120 ft. Ranged spell attack for 1d10 force.",
 "120 ft. You fling a dart of force at a creature or object in range. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit the target takes 1d10 force damage. It needs a prepared gauntlet worth at least 5 gp.\n\nThe damage rises by 1d10 at level 5, 11 and 17."],
"Force Weapon": ["Cantrip, 5 ft, 1 round. Melee spell attack for 1d10 force, then one opportunity attack with the blade. More attacks at levels 5, 11 and 17.",
 "5 ft, 1 round. You conjure a blade of force that lashes at your foes. Make a melee spell attack against a creature in range. On a hit it takes 1d10 force damage. Until the start of your next turn you can make a single strike with the blade as an opportunity attack. You make an extra attack on your turn at level 5 (2), 11 (3) and 17 (4). It needs a prepared gauntlet worth at least 5 gp."],
"Free Throw": ["Self, 1 round. Guide a thrown object (5 lb or less) up to 150 ft around obstacles. A creature hit takes 4d4 bludgeoning, Dexterity save for half.",
 "Self, 1 round. As part of casting, you throw a handheld object of 5 pounds or less. For the duration you steer its exact path up to 150 feet. It can go around obstacles and corners, and it ignores cover when aimed at a creature. A creature it hits makes a Dexterity save, taking 4d4 bludgeoning damage on a failure or half on a success. The object stops after hitting a creature or object." + HL + "The maximum weight rises by 5 pounds and the damage by 4d4 for each slot level above 1."],
"Frenzy": ["120 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. Creatures in 20 ft fail a Wisdom save and attack whatever is in reach, or themselves.",
 "120 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. You reduce a crowd to violent instinct. Choose a point you see. Each creature within 20 feet of it makes a Wisdom save. On a failure it is frenzied for the duration and draws a melee weapon if it has one. A frenzied creature must use its action at the start of its turn to attack a creature in reach, with a melee weapon if it has one, otherwise an improvised weapon or unarmed strike. With several targets in reach it picks one at random. With none, it attacks itself against its own AC and deals damage on a hit. At the end of its turn it can repeat the save to end the effect."],
"Frigid Blade": ["Cantrip, 5 ft, 1 round. Melee weapon attack with cold damage. If the target moves willingly, your Reaction deals 1d8 cold.",
 "5 ft, 1 round. As part of the casting action, make a melee weapon attack against a creature in range, or the spell fails. On a hit, the whole attack deals cold damage instead of its usual type, and the target is coated in brittle frost until the start of your next turn. If it willingly moves before then, you can use your Reaction to deal 1d8 cold damage to it, ending the spell.\n\nAt level 5, the attack and the secondary damage each deal an extra 1d8 cold damage. Both rise again at level 11 (2d8 and 3d8) and level 17 (3d8 and 4d8)."],
"Frolicking Fountain": ["120 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. A hypnotic 5 ft cube of water charms creatures within 60 ft and lashes for 4d6.",
 "120 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. You conjure a 5-foot cube of hypnotically swirling water in an empty space in range. It stays in place, sending small jets up to 5 feet into the air. Each creature other than you within 60 feet that sees it makes a Wisdom save or is charmed by you for the duration. A charmed creature must use its movement to get as close to the water as it can and cannot willingly move away. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns. A creature that succeeds cannot be affected by that casting again. When a creature is within 5 feet of the fountain, you can use a Bonus Action to make a melee spell attack against it, dealing 4d6 bludgeoning damage on a hit. A charmed target can save again after taking this damage."],
"Gahoul's Glorious Gothic": ["1 mile, 7 days, 1 hour cast. Summon a gothic manor with a vault, 50 skeleton servants and 3 ghouls. Permanent if recast weekly for a year.",
 "1 mile, 7 days, casting time 1 hour. A rift opens and tons of brick and stone assemble into a gothic estate: a manor with a vault, a 200-by-200-foot courtyard and a 10-foot wrought iron fence. Creatures in the area are escorted out by harmless but forceful specters.\n\nYou design the manor, up to 50 ten-foot cubes or five stories including basements, with barred windows and gargoyles, furnished as you choose. The layout is recorded in the manor miniature and cannot change later. The manor has 50 skeleton servants that obey you, can do any normal servant task but cannot attack or directly harm anyone, and enough food for 50 people a day for a week. It holds a 15-foot-cube extradimensional vault, and items placed in it are there the next time you cast the spell.\n\nThe courtyard is soaked in necromantic magic: any humanoid buried there rises 24 hours later as a ghoul under your control, as with Animate Dead. Three ghouls rise when you cast it. They cannot leave the estate and patrol it unless ordered otherwise. Undead cannot be turned inside it.\n\nAfter 7 days the estate falls to dust and bone, and items inside appear safely where it stood. Cast in the same place once every 7 days for a year, it becomes permanent."],
"Gahoul's Scapegoat": ["Self, 8 hours, 1 minute cast. Mark a willing creature within 5 ft. When you are hit, use your Reaction to swap places with it so it takes the hit.",
 "Self, 8 hours, casting time 1 minute. You trace a complex arcane symbol on a willing creature within 5 feet, marking it for sacrifice. For the duration, when an attack hits you and the marked creature is within 60 feet, you can use your Reaction to swap positions with it so that it is hit instead. The spell then ends."],
"Gahoul's Shrieking Skull": ["60 ft. A skull shrieks (heard 300 ft) and deals 2d4 thunder to everything in a 10 ft cube, no save.",
 "60 ft. You throw a cackling skull at a point you see. It emits a mortifying shriek audible to 300 feet. Each creature in a 10-foot cube centered on the skull takes 2d4 thunder damage, with no save." + HL + "The damage rises by 2d4 for each slot level above 1."],
"Gahoul's Spectral Scythe": ["60 ft, 1 round. A scythe flies in a 60 by 10 ft line for 6d8 necrotic (Dexterity save for half) and returns next turn.",
 "60 ft, 1 round. You conjure a phantom scythe and throw it whirling along a line 60 feet long and 10 feet wide. It stops at the end of the line or before solid objects and hovers there. Each creature in the area while it moves makes a Dexterity save, taking 6d8 necrotic damage on a failure or half on a success. A creature has Disadvantage if the scythe comes to rest in its space. If you are within 120 feet of the scythe at the start of your next turn, it flies back to you along a 10-foot-wide line, and creatures in its path save against the same damage." + HL + "The damage rises by 1d6 for each slot level above 6."],
"Game of Fate": ["60 ft, 1 hour. Compel a creature to a game with stakes. The loser takes 6d6 psychic damage, and bets can raise it to 10d6.",
 "60 ft, 1 hour. You compel a creature in range to play a nonmagical game with vital consequences. It is unaffected if its Intelligence is 3 or lower or if it speaks no language. An unwilling creature makes a Wisdom save to resist. If it fails, it joins the game. If the target takes damage or falls unconscious, the spell ends. The loser takes 6d6 psychic damage. If nobody wins or loses by the end of the duration, you and the target both take it.\n\nYou and the target can negotiate higher stakes: more psychic damage up to 10d6, property, or odder rewards such as a title. The spell reveals if someone bets property they do not own. A bet is sealed by a handshake or similar gesture. Property bet is teleported to the winner at the end, and the loser is compelled to carry out any promised action. No outside spell, effect or creature can influence the game."],
"Geomantic Discernment": ["100 ft, Concentration, 10 minutes. You see valuable minerals, metals and gems glow within 100 ft, through any nonmagical material.",
 "100 ft, Concentration, 10 minutes. You sense valuable minerals in a 100-foot radius. A glowing aura only you can see appears around valuable metals, gems, ores, native elements and similar resources there for the duration. You see it through any amount of nonmagical material."],
"Glitterdust": ["15 ft cone, Concentration, 1 minute. Constitution save or blinded, and everyone in the cone loses invisibility.",
 "15-foot cone, Concentration, 1 minute. You spray golden particles over everything in the cone. Each creature makes a Constitution save or is blinded for the duration, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns. Every creature in the area, saved or not, cannot benefit from being invisible for the duration."],
"Grasp of the Grave": ["120 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. Skeletal arms fill a 20 ft radius as difficult terrain and deal 3d6 necrotic (Strength save), dragging creatures.",
 "120 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. Spectral skeletal arms rise from the ground in a 20-foot-radius circle at a point you see and grasp at creatures. Undead ignore the spell. The area is difficult terrain. When a creature enters the area for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, it makes a Strength save. On a failure it takes 3d6 necrotic damage and is dragged to any unoccupied space in the area you choose. On a success it takes half damage and is not moved. Until the spell ends you can use your action to make each creature in the area save at once." + HL + "The damage rises by 3d6 for each slot level above 4."],
"Guided Missile": ["Bonus Action, self, Concentration, 1 minute. Your next ranged weapon attack has Advantage and doubled ranges.",
 "Self, Concentration, 1 minute. You pray over your projectile so it arcs to its mark. Your next ranged weapon attack before the spell ends has Advantage and double its normal and long range."],
"Halo of Flame": ["10 ft. A 10 ft radius ring of fire around you deals 4d6 fire to creatures you choose (Dexterity save for half).",
 "10 ft. A ring of flame ignites above your head and springs outward into a burning circle: a 5-foot-wide line of fire forming a 10-foot-radius ring around you. Each creature you choose in the area makes a Dexterity save, taking 4d6 fire damage on a failure or half on a success." + HL + "The damage rises by 4d6 for each slot level above 2."],
"Hangover": ["30 ft. Constitution save or 3d8 psychic, Disadvantage on concentration saves from it, and poisoned until your next turn.",
 "30 ft. You emit a drunken aura that washes away into the feeling of an intense hangover. A creature you choose in range makes a Constitution save or takes 3d8 psychic damage. The target has Disadvantage on Constitution saves to maintain concentration on a spell because of this damage. On a failure it is also poisoned until the start of your next turn." + HL + "The damage rises by 3d8 for each slot level above 2."],
"Hardlight Blaster": ["10 ft. Conjure a floating blaster that shoots a ranged spell attack for 3d6 force from its own position.",
 "10 ft. You conjure a weapon of compressed light that hovers in an empty space within 10 feet. It fires a beam at a target you choose within 60 feet of it, as a ranged spell attack using your spell attack bonus. The weapon is the origin, so it can target a creature outside your line of sight if the weapon can see it. On a hit the target takes 3d6 force damage. The weapon then dissipates." + HL + "You deal an extra 1d6 lightning damage for each slot level above 1."],
"Hardlight Gauntlet": ["Touch. Three melee spell attacks deal 1d12, 2d12 and 3d12 force on the first, second and third hit.",
 "Touch. You conjure a gauntlet of compressed energy and unleash a barrage. Make three melee spell attacks against one target. The first hit deals 1d12 force damage, the second 2d12 and the third 3d12." + HL + "With a 5th-level slot or higher you make one extra attack, and the fourth hit deals 4d12. With a 7th-level slot or higher you make two extra attacks, and the fifth hit deals 5d12."],
}
